# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# StageZero Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and update values for your environment
# DO NOT commit .env to source control

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATABASE (SQLite)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SQLite database path (used in Docker)
DATABASE_PATH=/app/data/stagezero.db

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# APPLICATION
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# HTTPS CERTIFICATE (Docker only)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Password for the HTTPS certificate (.volumes/https/aspnetapp.pfx)
# See .volumes/https/README.md for certificate setup instructions
CERT_PASSWORD=STRONG_PASSWORD

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EMAIL (SMTP)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SMTP server for the verification and password-reset codes the login pages send.
# Leave these commented out to run without email: the codes are then written to the
# application log (`docker logs <container>` in Docker) and the pages say so.
# Email__SmtpHost and Email__FromEmail are the minimum; the app logs its email status
# at startup ("Email: sending through ..." or "Email: ... not set").
#
# For Gmail:
# 1. Enable 2-factor authentication on your Google account
# 2. Generate an App Password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
# 3. Use the App Password (not your regular password) as Email__SmtpPassword
#
# Note: Use double underscores (__) for nested configuration
# Email__SmtpHost=smtp.gmail.com
# Email__SmtpPort=587
# Email__SmtpUsername=your-email@gmail.com
# Email__SmtpPassword=your-app-password
# Email__FromEmail=your-email@gmail.com
# Email__FromName=StageZero
#
# STARTTLS is on by default and is what Gmail, Outlook and every public relay expect.
# Set it to false only for a plaintext relay on a trusted network (a local Postfix,
# MailHog, or a mail sidecar in the same compose stack); leave the username and
# password unset for a relay that does not authenticate.
# Email__UseStartTls=true

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL (OPTIONAL — DOCKER SIDECAR ONLY)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Only needed if you run the cloudflared connector as a container instead of a
# host service. Get the token from StageZero's Tunnel Setup page, then start the
# stack with:
#   docker compose -f prod.docker-compose.yml --profile tunnel up -d
#
# Running cloudflared as a host service (macOS launchd / Windows service /
# systemd) is the recommended setup — the connector then survives the app stack
# going down. See ..Documentation/CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_SETUP.md.
#
# Treat this like a password: it grants the ability to serve traffic on your
# tunnel's hostnames.
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Example project with real SMTP data
# StageZero